  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "See recent report on dev list from Richard Jones for Fedora 3.2",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Reproduced on 3.2.1 and on the trunk (post RELS-INT integration).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Richard reports that adding a new RELS-EXT datastream using the REST API with a dateTime literal that is invalid, eg 2009-10-05T16:02:26+0100, is not validated.  However updating the datastream (eg adding a new relationship) then results in a validation error.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Reproduced using the admin client (so this is not limited to the REST API): create a new object, add RELS-EXT with invalid date time, does not result in a validation error.  However subsequently amending RELS-EXT does throw a validation error.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The bug is not limited to dateTime, this also occurs for integer values (eg 1.23 is allowed), and also occurs when adding relationships with predicates that are not allowed in RELS-EXT, so it would appear that RELS-EXT is not validated at all when it is created for the first time.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
